# Citation metadata (Citation File Format). GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository".
# `doi` is the Zenodo version DOI of the v1.0.0 release; the concept DOI (all versions) is in
# `identifiers`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Graph Digitizer"
abstract: >-
  A client-side graph digitizer: load a chart image, calibrate the axes from two known points
  each (linear, log, reciprocal, date/time) by hand or with tick-label OCR, trace plotted
  series or place points by hand on one or more lines, and export the table. Images never
  leave the browser.
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Brian Mark
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2748-1444"
    affiliation: "University of California San Diego"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/brianmanderson/BMAnderson_GraphDigitizer"
url: "https://brianmanderson.github.io/BMAnderson_GraphDigitizer/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24092762"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24092762"
    description: "Zenodo archive of version 1.0.0 (git tag v1.0.0)"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24092761"
    description: "Concept DOI: all versions, resolves to the latest"
keywords:
  - graph digitizer
  - plot digitizer
  - figure data extraction
  - Kaplan-Meier
  - axis detection
  - OCR
